\caption(The diagram shows actual final metadata: two trie nodes and ten leaf buckets. The root a slot is a child edge, not a nine-string leaf that somehow remains after its burst. Equal apple strings retain their original input-id order.)
\alttext(A blue root points to a blue child for prefix a and six green root buckets for b through g. The a child points to green buckets al, ap, ar and av, with counts one, six, one and one.)

Insertion follows one byte at a time. A leaf slot holds original string ids;
when it overflows, a new child consumes the slot byte and receives those ids
in their actual encounter order. Strings ending at a node go into its separate
terminal list. Collection emits terminals first, then slots in unsigned byte
order. A leaf is sorted by full string value, with original id breaking equal
value ties; a child is traversed before the next byte slot. This produces
ordinary byte-lexicographic order, with prefixes before their extensions.

The old sorting_dist include remains a compatibility entry point. The ordinary
one-argument API keeps its threshold eight. A separate configured entry point
accepts a positive capacity and an optional whole-call node cap. No overload
ambiguity is introduced for existing function-pointer or callback uses.

> Preserve the first-letter plot and vary capacity

The root slot's strings field counts its actual represented subtree, whether
it is a leaf or a child. It reproduces the original counts a:9, b:2, c:3,
d:1, e:1, f:1 and g:2. The child field independently confirms which slot
burst; the report does not turn a histogram into a guessed trie.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/burstsort.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::string> words{
      "banana","apple","apricot","avocado","blueberry","cherry","cranberry","coconut",
      "date","elderberry","fig","grape","guava","apple","apex","april","apply","arc","almond"};
  const auto original=dm::algorithms::burstsort_trace(words);
  std::vector<double> heights;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| actual root byte slot | represented strings | child exists |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (const auto& slot:original.slots) if (slot.node==0) {
    heights.push_back(slot.strings);labels.push_back(std::string(1,static_cast<char>(slot.value)));
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",static_cast<char>(slot.value),slot.strings,slot.child!=0);
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(heights,labels,"root slot count",dm::RGB{124,58,237})
      .abline_h(8.0,dm::RGB{220,38,38},1.5)
      .title("Original root slots: only a bursts at capacity eight")
      .x_label("first byte").y_label("strings represented by root slot").y_limits(0,12)
      .size(1100,520).save_svg("build/burstsort.svg");
  std::print("\n| capacity B | trie nodes | actual bursts | deepest node | routing byte reads | leaf sort calls | directory slot checks |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const std::size_t capacity:{1,2,4,8,16}) {
    dm::algorithms::BurstSortOptions options;options.bucket_capacity=capacity;
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::burstsort_trace(words,options);
    if (trace.output!=original.output) return 1;
    for (const auto& slot:trace.slots) if (!slot.child && slot.strings>capacity) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",capacity,trace.nodes.size(),trace.bursts.size(),trace.max_depth,
        trace.byte_routes,trace.leaf_comparisons,trace.collection_slot_scans);
  }
}
