// result_end
\caption(The original purple root-slot counts and red capacity-eight line are retained. Bursting is strict: a slot of size eight remains a leaf, while size nine creates a child. The capacity sweep measures structure and logical work, not cache misses or elapsed speed.)
\alttext(The a root slot has nine strings and exceeds the red line at eight. The other root slots contain two, three, one, one, one and two strings, with no child nodes.)

Smaller capacities create more structure and more directory scans, while
larger capacities leave more full-string sorting inside leaves. The counts
alone cannot select a universal fastest threshold. In this implementation,
full string comparisons may revisit already shared prefixes; their invocation
count is not a byte-inspection count. std::sort call counts can also differ
between toolchains. The published [Sinha and Zobel study](https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/jzobel/fulltext/acmjea04.pdf)
examines cache-conscious implementations and workloads; its measured speedups
are not measurements of this C++ variant or these nineteen strings.

> A discontinuity: eight copies versus nine copies of a long string

For capacity B=8, eight identical strings remain in one root bucket. For nine
copies of a length-L string, each occupied slot overflows, creating another
child until the strings terminate. The final chain has L+1 nodes, including
the root, L bursts, and nine terminal ids at depth L. It is not a shallow trie.

Each original id consumes each routed prefix byte only once, including later
redistribution. For this duplicate family the actual counts are

\[
Q=L+1,\qquad R=9L,\qquad V=9(L+1),\qquad S=256(L+1),
\]

where Q is node count, R is routing-byte reads, V is insertion work items,
and S is collection directory checks. The factor 256 comes from this variant's
dense byte directories, even when a node has only one occupied slot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/burstsort_prefix_depth.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> length,flat_nodes,chain_nodes;
  std::print("| shared string length L | nodes for 8 copies | nodes for 9 copies | 9-copy bursts | 8-copy routes | 9-copy routes | 9-copy visits | 9-copy directory checks |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const std::size_t n:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512}) {
    const auto eight=dm::algorithms::burstsort_trace(std::vector<std::string>(8,std::string(n,'q')));
    const auto nine=dm::algorithms::burstsort_trace(std::vector<std::string>(9,std::string(n,'q')));
    if (eight.nodes.size()!=1 || !eight.bursts.empty() || eight.byte_routes!=8 ||
        nine.nodes.size()!=n+1 || nine.bursts.size()!=n || nine.max_depth!=n || nine.byte_routes!=9*n ||
        nine.insertion_visits!=9*(n+1) || nine.collection_slot_scans!=256*(n+1) || nine.leaf_comparisons!=0) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,eight.nodes.size(),nine.nodes.size(),nine.bursts.size(),
        eight.byte_routes,nine.byte_routes,nine.insertion_visits,nine.collection_slot_scans);
    length.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(n)));
    flat_nodes.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(eight.nodes.size())));
    chain_nodes.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(nine.nodes.size())));
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .lines(length,flat_nodes,"8 copies",dm::RGB{37,99,235},2).points(length,flat_nodes,"",dm::RGB{37,99,235},4)
      .lines(length,chain_nodes,"9 copies",dm::RGB{220,38,38},2).points(length,chain_nodes,"",dm::RGB{220,38,38},4)
      .title("Eight copies stay flat; nine build a prefix chain")
      .x_label("log2(shared string length L)").y_label("log2(actual trie node count)").y_limits(-0.5,12)
      .size(1100,520).save_svg("build/burstsort_prefix_depth.svg");
}
```
